.658, 40.682]}, "quality_check": null, "script_sha256": "6739844989b2ea8cb127e1ca245d384a4c035053ad0113a4823967613b8b9362", "text": "That is why I understand the emotion behind his old joke about a parade if titles were ever reassigned. It put a football feeling into an absurd image. Years later, everyone gathering to celebrate something they never got to celebrate together at the time. But would it feel the same? Could a changed record recreate the roar when the whistle goes and you know you have done it? Could it put that version of Klopp back on the touchline, with those players, in front of those supporters? No. A trophy can be presented later. A table can be rewritten. The moment cannot. That does not make accountability pointless. It makes timely accountability more important. A sport that takes years to settle its biggest questions leaves the people who lived through them carrying the uncertainty.", "voice_id": "bu5eKETbFKC8G702EAU4", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2"}